The high-spin to low-spin crossover for octahedral d⁴ at B = 706 cm⁻¹ and C = 2734 cm⁻¹ is at **Dq ≈ 1675 cm⁻¹** (Δ = 10·Dq ≈ 16 755 cm⁻¹, Dq/B ≈ 2.37).

I got this from the spin-crossover tool, which compares the ground-term energies of the quartet (high-spin) and doublet (low-spin) states across the Dq sweep. The high-spin ground term stays at zero energy until the low-spin ground term drops to meet it at that point. Below Dq ≈ 1675 cm⁻¹ the ion is high-spin; above it, low-spin.

